506	1135,405,1700,960	503. Flower of Trillium, natural size.	A six-parted flower seen from above: three broad pointed petals alternating with three narrower sepals, the six stamens with long anthers around the central pistil.
508	110,1425,245,2178	508. Pistil, magnified; the ovary cut across.	A single pistil with a long slender style rising from a rounded ovary; below it the ovary cut across, showing its three cells.
507	305,1760,740,2180	507. Flower of Spiderwort.	A flower of three broad rounded petals on a short stalk, with six stamens bearded with jointed hairs clustered at the centre.
